oom Family Timeline","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"title":"About the Authors","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}}],"weight":"9.6 ounces","subject_place":["Netherlands","Germany","Ravensbrück.","Netherlands."],"covers":[562527],"lc_classifications":["D805.5.R38 T46 2006","D805.5.R38T46 2006"],"contributions":["Sherrill, Elizabeth.","Sherrill, John L."],"subject_time":["German occupation, 1949-1945."],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"genres":["Personal narratives, Dutch."],"contributors":[{"role":"Foreword","name":"Joni Eareckson Tada"},{"role":"Preface","name":"Elizabeth Sherrill"},{"role":"Introduction","name":"Andrew van der Bijl"}],"source_records":["amazon:0800794052","bwb:9780800794057","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part32.utf8:145937534:1517","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2022-06-13"],"title":"The Hiding Place","edition_name":"35th anniversary ed.","subjects":["Ten Boom, Corrie.","Ravensbrück (Concentration camp)","World War, 1939-1945 -- Concentration camps -- Germany -- Ravensbrück.","World War, 1939-1945 -- Underground movements -- Netherlands.","World War, 1939-1945 -- Personal narratives, Dutch.","Netherlands -- History -- German occupation, 1949-1945."],"publish_country":"miu","by_statement":"Corrie ten Boom with John and Elizabeth Sherrill.","type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"uris":["http://www.loc.gov/catdir/toc/ecip0518/2005023916.html"],"physical_dimensions":"8.5 x 5.5 x 0.6 inches","publishers":["Chosen Books"],"description":"Corrie ten Boom was a Dutch watchmaker who became a heroine of the Resistance, a survivor of Hitler's concentration camps, and one of the most remarkable evangelists of the twentieth century. In World War II she and her family risked their lives to help Jews and underground workers escape from the Nazis, and for their work they were tested in the infamous Nazi death camps. Only Corrie among her family survived to tell the story of how faith ultimately triumphs over evil.\r\n\r\nHere is the riveting account of how Corrie and her family were able to save many of God's chosen people. For 35 years millions have seen that there is no pit so deep that God's love is not deeper still. Now The Hiding Place, repackaged for a new generation of readers, continues to declare that God's love will overcome, heal, and restore.","dewey_decimal_class":["940.53/492/092"],"physical_format":"Paperback","key":"/books/OL3408070M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL229401A","name":"Corrie ten Boom"}],"publish_places":["Grand Rapids, MI"],"pagination":"p. cm.","uri_descriptions":["Table of contents"],"classifications":{},"url":["http://www.loc.gov/catdir/toc/ecip0518/2005023916.html"],"identifiers":{"goodreads":["272676"],"librarything":["2247"]},"lccn":["2005023916"],"isbn_10":["0800794052"],"publish_date":"2006","works":[{"key":"/works/OL1915012W"}],"local_id":["urn:bwbsku:W7-CWR-088"],"latest_revision":15,"revision":15,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-01T03:28:50.625462"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2022-12-05T02:34:58.144912"}}},"OLID:OL5417838M":{"bib_key":"OLID:OL5417838M","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL5417838M/The_hiding_place","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL5417838M/The_hiding_place","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13588284-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["G. K. Hall"],"identifiers":{"goodreads":["3512977"],"librarything":["2247"]},"local_id":["urn:sfpl:31223041795148"],"lc_classifications":["D811.5 .T427 1973"],"key":"/books/OL5417838M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL229401A","name":"Corrie ten Boom"}],"publish_places":["Boston"],"contributions":["Sherrill, John L., joint author.","Sherrill, Elizabeth, joint author."],"subjects":["Ten Boom, Corrie.","Ravensbrück (Concentration camp)","World War, 1939-1945 -- Personal narratives, Dutch.","Large type books."],"pagination":"431 p.","source_records":["marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run01.mrc:2108037